The R36S's known panels, as overlays for ROCKNIX's generic-dsi driver
(plastron's kernel patch 4-rocknix-panel-generic-dsi.patch). The card's boot
partition holds them all as overlays/panel-NAME.dtbo, and r36s-boot.txt's
zy_panel=NAME picks one (board/r36s/boot-prelude.cmd). Without it, the
card's device tree drives panel 0, the first R36S's.

Each panel-NAME.dts is what plastron/scripts/r36s-panel.py writes from that
panel's stock device tree, and panel-NAME.dtbo is dtc's build of it. The
facts each one holds (the panel's init sequence, its mode, its size, its DSI
lanes and flags) come from the stock device trees in lcdyk0517/arkos4clone
(MIT), commit 94d5431f070857736ae2ebe40e567608a08db47d,
boot/dArkOS/consoles/:

  panel-0     origin panel0/rk3326-r36s-panel0-linux.dtb         ST7703
  panel-1     origin panel1/rk3326-r36s-panel1-linux.dtb         unknown (E0 AB BA)
  panel-2     origin panel2/rk3326-r36s-panel2-linux.dtb         NV3051D
  panel-3     origin panel3/rk3326-r36s-panel3-linux.dtb         NV3051D
  panel-4     origin panel4 type1/rk3326-r36s-panel4-type1-linux.dtb  NV3051D
  panel-4v22  origin panel4 type2/rk3326-r36s-panel4-type2-linux.dtb  NV3051D, board V22

Two have the same init sequence in a tree under the GPL too: panel 0 in
ArkOS's kernel, christianhaitian/linux branch rg351,
arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r35s-linux.dts ((GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)), and
panel 4v22 in sudowaffles/dtb-r36s-v30-20251811, dts/rk3326-r36s-linux.dts
(GPL-2.0). The waits at power-up and the DSI clock flag are the ones that lit
board R36S-V12's panel 4 (r36s-panel.py says which). Panel 5 (an ST7703
with other timings) has none yet: no stock tree for it under a license
that lets it be copied.

To make one again:

    python3 plastron/scripts/r36s-panel.py STOCK.dtb \
        plastron/buildroot/board/r36s/overlays/panel-NAME.dtbo
